<topic id="alerts">
  <title>Alerts</title>
  <shortdesc>Provide contextual feedback messages for typical user actions with the handful of available and flexible
    alert messages.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Alerts</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlatt>otherprops</xmlatt></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>note</xmlelement></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>section</xmlelement></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section>
      <title>Example</title>
      <p>Alerts are available for any length of text, as well as an optional close button. For proper styling, use one
        of the eight required contextual classes (e.g., set <xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt> to
          <codeph>alert-success</codeph>).</p>
    </section>
    <fig>
      <title>Alerts</title>
      <image href="src/alerts-1.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/basic.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/alerts/basic.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section>
      <title>Additional content</title>
      <p>Alerts can also contain additional HTML elements like headings, paragraphs, icons and links.</p>
    </section>
    <fig>
      <title>Additional content</title>
      <image href="src/alerts-2.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/additional-content.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/alerts/additional-content.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section>
      <title>Notes</title>
      <p>DITA <xmlelement>note</xmlelement> elements are displayed as alerts according to the <xmlatt>type</xmlatt>
        attribute. With the exception <xmlatt>type="othertype"</xmlatt>, an icon is added if <xmlatt
        >type</xmlatt> is present.</p>
    </section>
    <fig>
      <title>Notes</title>
      <image href="src/alerts-3.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <codeblock>&lt;note type="note"&gt;
  This is just a note.
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="notice"&gt;
  Notice this piece of information.
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="fastpath"&gt;
  This note will speed you on your way.
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="remember"&gt;
  Don't forget to do what this note says.
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="tip"&gt;
  This is a fine little tip.
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="attention"&gt;
  Please pay extra attention to this note.
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="caution"&gt;
  Care is required when proceeding.
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="important"&gt;
  This note is important.
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="restriction"&gt;
  You can't do what this note says.
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="danger"&gt;
  You may hurt yourself!
&lt;/note&gt;
&lt;note type="other" othertype="Another note"&gt;
  This is something other than a normal note.
&lt;/note&gt;</codeblock>
    <p>The default colors can be overridden by using a <xmlatt>color</xmlatt> attribute or an <xmlatt
      >outputclass</xmlatt>.</p>
    <fig>
      <title>Colored Notes</title>
      <image href="src/alerts-4.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/note-colors.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/alerts/note-colors.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <p>Use an additional <xmlatt>icon</xmlatt> attribute or <xmlatt>otherprops</xmlatt> to alter the default icon.</p>
    <fig>
      <title>Notes with altered icons</title>
      <image href="src/alerts-5.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/note-icons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/alerts/note-icons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
  </body>
</topic>
